# @io/secrets/sops — the SOPS (Secrets OPerationS) vendor
# projection sub-species under @io/secrets.
#
# Sub-species under @io/secrets at the vendor-tool altitude; the
# FIRST concrete projection method Alex named in the 2026-07-14
# SSH-signing design intent ("@secrets prism and @secrets/sops to
# project visibility/private stuff onto disk through the Peers
# key"). Sibling to future `@io/secrets/age`, `@io/secrets/vault`,
# `@io/secrets/1password` sub-species.
#
# === Landing metadata ===
#
# Landed 2026-07-15 by Mara as Landing 5 of the @secrets shape-
# proposal sequence (companion audit: `docs/audits/2026-07-15-
# seam-secrets-shape-proposal-phase-d-cascade.md` at 019ad8f;
# verdict SEAM-RATIFY Candidate 2 with sub-species per §D8:
# "@io/secrets carries the peer-key-gated projection primitive;
# @io/secrets/sops carries SOPS-specific realization"; sub-species
# specializes parent's carrier — secret_projection concretizes
# as sops_file_ref). Companion shape-proposal at `docs/scouts/
# 2026-07-15-mara-secrets-shape-proposal.md` §2.7 (SOPS sub-
# species substrate-decl).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent (verbatim) ===
#
# From `shards/subject/visibility/sheaf.mirror` 21-32:
#
#   "@secrets prism and @secrets/sops to project visibility/private
#    stuff onto disk through the Peers key."
#
# Alex explicitly named @secrets/sops as SPECIES alongside
# @secrets prism. Per shape-proposal §5.4: sub-species pattern
# admits sibling projection methods; SOPS is the first.
#
# === What SOPS IS ===
#
# SOPS (Secrets OPerationS): originally created by Julien Vehent
# at Mozilla (2017); rewritten to Go in v3.x (2020+); currently
# maintained by the CNCF at github.com/getsops/sops (per Seam
# §D2.a REED-INLINE cascade b: vendor-language corrected from
# "Python" to "Go"; under-@io conclusion unchanged per io.mirror
# 37-40 Glass Wall). Vendor tool that encrypts YAML/JSON files
# in-place using recipient-based key groups: age keys, PGP keys,
# AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault, HashiCorp Vault Transit.
#
# Load-bearing SOPS discipline for this sub-species:
#
#   - IN-PLACE encryption: keys stay in plaintext; values get
#     encrypted per-leaf. Structure preserved for diff/merge.
#   - RECIPIENT lists: each SOPS-encrypted file names its recipient
#     key group; each recipient can independently decrypt.
#   - ROUND-TRIP fidelity: sops_decrypt ∘ sops_encrypt IS byte-
#     identity on the section (modulo key ordering which SOPS
#     preserves per the underlying JSON/YAML emitter).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Per shape-proposal §0.3 + §2.7 verified:
#
#   1. Alex 2026-07-14 verbatim naming (sheaf.mirror 30-32) —
#      "@secrets/sops" named as species alongside "@secrets prism."
#
#   2. `shards/io.mirror` 37-40 Glass Wall — SOPS is vendor tool
#      (Go, YAML/JSON-encrypted files, in-place edits); under-@io
#      per family-root discipline.
#
#   3. `shards/io.mirror` 161-162 — age named as vendor surface
#      under @io/crypto; age IS one of SOPS's primary key backends.
#
#   4. `shards/mirror/data/yaml.mirror` + `shards/mirror/data/
#      json.mirror` — LANDED shards (2026-06-07; verified per
#      Seam §D8 REED-INLINE cascade c: dependency verification
#      confirmed shards exist at claimed mount points).
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @io                       — family-root; boundary discipline.
#   @io/secrets               — parent species; sub-species
#                               specializes secret_projection as
#                               sops_file_ref; specializes project
#                               as sops_encrypt; specializes
#                               retrieve as sops_decrypt.
#   @io/crypto                — provides age_encrypt / age_decrypt
#                               for age-backend recipients;
#                               provides ed25519_verify for signed
#                               SOPS metadata.
#   @mirror/data/yaml         — YAML wire format (sops_encrypt/
#                               decrypt over .sops.yaml files).
#   @mirror/data/json         — JSON wire format (sops_encrypt/
#                               decrypt over .sops.json files).
#
# Bound per shape-proposal §2.7:
#
#   - Does NOT re-declare YAML/JSON (composes over @mirror/data/
#     yaml + json).
#   - Does NOT re-declare age/pgp/kms crypto (composes over
#     @io/crypto).
#   - Does NOT carry the sops binary itself (opaque per @io;
#     carries the CONTRACT the binary discharges).
#
# Species specialization pattern @io/cargo established: declare
# vendor-tool contract; runtime opaque-executes.
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
# - shards/io/secrets.mirror (parent species landed alongside).
# - shards/io/crypto.mirror (sibling; age vendor surface).
# - shards/mirror/data/yaml.mirror + json.mirror (composition
#   parents; landed 2026-06-07).
# - docs/scouts/2026-07-15-mara-secrets-shape-proposal.md §2.7
#   (the sub-species substrate-decl this shard discharges).
# - docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-secrets-shape-proposal-phase-d-
#   cascade.md §D8 (SOPS sub-species scope-fit verdict PASS with
#   REED-INLINE dependency verification pre-applied).
# - SOPS project (github.com/getsops/sops) — Mozilla 2017;
#   CNCF-maintained; v3.x Go rewrite 2020+.
# - age (age-encryption.org) — Valsorda 2019+; SOPS's primary
#   key backend.
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (`prism
#   @io/secrets/sops`),
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (transparency
#   inheritance through @io + @io/secrets),
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (SOPS lifts as sub-species
#   under the @io/secrets carrier per Alex 2026-07-14 verbatim),
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (Alex named
#   "@secrets/sops" explicitly; substrate-decl names what the
#   design intent already contained),
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (sops_file_ref, sops_key_group,
#   sops_metadata are typed carriers; never bare refs),
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (all action bodies `\`-obligation-
#   blocked; consumers pull the realization; Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR
#   pending),
# [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]] (composition-only over
#   @io/secrets + @io/crypto + @mirror/data; NO Rust extension;
#   sops binary invocation is opaque @io per parent discipline).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/io/secrets/sops.
# mirror` declares `@io/secrets/sops` per `@epistemologic/pact/
# path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-07-14-ssh-signing-design-intent
source @arxiv/security/vehent-2017-sops
source @arxiv/security/valsorda-2019-age

prism @io/secrets/sops {
  focus  sops_file_ref
  project sops_file_ref
  split  sops_file_ref
  shift  sops_file_ref
  settle sops_file_ref
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === The sops_file_ref carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for an on-disk SOPS-encrypted YAML/JSON file.
# Per SOPS format (github.com/getsops/sops/README §File-format):
# a well-formed YAML/JSON document whose values are per-leaf-
# encrypted with the recipient key group, plus a `sops` metadata
# section carrying the recipient list + integrity MAC.
#
# Opaque foreign blob per @io family-root Glass Wall discipline;
# substrate carries the ref, not the bytes.
#
# Four-field record:
#
#   on_disk_path — @io/fs.path carrier naming the file's location
#                  (typically .sops.yaml or a section-encrypted
#                  named file).
#   wire_format  — typed ref naming YAML or JSON (per @mirror/data
#                  species; determines which parser the sops
#                  binary dispatches).
#   metadata     — typed ref to the sops_metadata carrier (below);
#                  carries the recipient list + integrity witness.
#   ciphertext_bytes
#                — typed ref to the encrypted-values byte payload
#                  (opaque; parsed only via sops binary).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (on_disk_path, wire_format,
# metadata, ciphertext_bytes).
type sops_file_ref = {
  on_disk_path:     ref,
  wire_format:      ref,
  metadata:         ref,
  ciphertext_bytes: ref,
}

# === The sops_key_group carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for a SOPS recipient key group. Per SOPS
# recipient discipline: each SOPS-encrypted file names its
# recipient set; each recipient in the set can independently
# decrypt via their private key.
#
# Three-field record:
#
#   age_recipients — typed ref to the list of age recipients
#                    (X25519 or ssh-ed25519 public keys per
#                    age-encryption.org; composes over @io/
#                    crypto.age_encrypt).
#   pgp_recipients — typed ref to the list of PGP public-key
#                    fingerprints. Refs into out-of-substrate
#                    keyring per @io opacity discipline.
#   kms_recipients — typed ref to the list of KMS recipient IDs
#                    (AWS KMS ARN, GCP KMS resource path, Azure
#                    Key Vault URI, HashiCorp Vault Transit key
#                    reference).
#
# Any of the three lists MAY be empty; the combined recipient
# set (union) MUST be non-empty per SOPS discipline (otherwise
# ciphertext is undecryptable).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (age_recipients,
# pgp_recipients, kms_recipients).
type sops_key_group = {
  age_recipients: ref,
  pgp_recipients: ref,
  kms_recipients: ref,
}

# === The sops_metadata carrier ===
#
# Typed reference for the `sops` metadata block SOPS appends to
# every encrypted file. Per SOPS format §metadata: carries the
# recipient list, per-key encrypted data key, integrity MAC,
# unencrypted-regex/encrypted-regex policy.
#
# Three-field record:
#
#   key_group      — the sops_key_group carrier (recipient list).
#   integrity_mac  — @io/crypto.signature_bytes or MAC ref carrying
#                    the integrity witness (SOPS uses SHA512 HMAC
#                    per its integrity discipline; the substrate
#                    carries the ref).
#   encryption_policy
#                  — typed ref naming which leaf keys/regexes are
#                    encrypted (SOPS's `encrypted_regex` +
#                    `unencrypted_regex` policy fields).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (key_group, integrity_mac,
# encryption_policy).
type sops_metadata = {
  key_group:         sops_key_group,
  integrity_mac:     ref,
  encryption_policy: ref,
}

# ============================================================
# §3 The actions
# ============================================================

# === sops_encrypt action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SOPS-encrypt action. Given a substrate section
# (typed ref to a YAML or JSON document from @mirror/data/yaml or
# @mirror/data/json) and a sops_key_group, produce a sops_file_
# ref: run the SOPS encryption pipeline (per-leaf age/pgp/kms
# encryption + integrity MAC + metadata assembly), return the
# typed reference.
#
# requires sops_key_group_admissible(kg): the key group MUST have
# at least one recipient AND every recipient MUST be well-formed
# per its backend (age recipients per @io/crypto.recipients_
# admissible; PGP/KMS refs per their species discipline).
#
# Returns imperfect<sops_file_ref, ref, ref>:
# - success(sops_file_ref) — encryption complete; the returned
#   sops_file_ref is decryptable by any recipient in kg.
# - partial(sops_file_ref, transparency) — encryption complete
#   with residual (e.g., a KMS recipient was unreachable but the
#   age recipients succeeded; ciphertext is partially-usable).
# - failure(error, transparency) — encryption failed (all
#   recipients unreachable, sops binary invocation failed,
#   section not YAML/JSON-parseable).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary (sops binary +
# vendor crypto per recipient backend; permanent-@io per
# glass-wall partition).
sops_encrypt(section: ref, key_group: sops_key_group) -> imperfect { \ }

# === sops_decrypt action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SOPS-decrypt action. Inverse of sops_encrypt.
# Given a sops_file_ref and a decryption key (@io/crypto.
# key_material for the recipient's private key), run the SOPS
# decryption pipeline: verify integrity MAC, decrypt data key
# via recipient backend, decrypt per-leaf values, reassemble
# the plaintext section.
#
# requires key_material_admissible(k): the decryption key MUST
# be well-formed per @io/crypto discipline.
#
# Returns imperfect<ref, ref, ref>:
# - success(section_ref) — decryption complete; section_ref
#   resolves to the plaintext YAML/JSON section bytes.
# - failure(error, transparency) — decryption failed (key not in
#   recipient list, integrity MAC mismatch, ciphertext tampered,
#   wire format parse error).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
sops_decrypt(f: sops_file_ref, k: key_material) -> imperfect { \ }

# === sops_key_group_from_sheaf_restriction action ===
#
# THE composition bridge action. Given a @subject/visibility/
# sheaf.sheaf_restriction, project its peer_ref → ACL binding
# into a sops_key_group: enumerate the peers admitted by the ACL,
# resolve each peer's key material to its age/pgp/kms recipient
# form, assemble the sops_key_group.
#
# THIS IS THE ARROW that connects @subject/visibility/sheaf (ACL
# structure) to @io/secrets/sops (SOPS recipient list). Per
# shape-proposal §2.7 verbatim: "composition bridge: @sheaf ACL
# projects into SOPS key-group ACL."
#
# requires restriction_admissible(sr): the restriction MUST be
# well-formed per @subject/visibility/sheaf discipline.
#
# Returns imperfect<sops_key_group, ref, ref>:
# - success(sops_key_group) — key group assembled; every admitted
#   peer's key material has been resolved into a recipient form.
# - partial(sops_key_group, transparency) — key group assembled
#   with residual (some peers had unresolvable key material;
#   opacity carries the missing peer list).
# - failure(error, transparency) — bridge failed (restriction
#   references peers with no key material; ACL structure not
#   projectable).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; composes @io/
# crypto.ssh_key_material for peer-key resolution.
sops_key_group_from_sheaf_restriction(sr: sheaf_restriction) -> imperfect { \ }

# === sops_round_trip action ===
#
# Discipline action per @io/secrets.round_trip pattern:
# sops_encrypt + sops_decrypt, verify recovered plaintext byte-
# equals the original section. Per shape-proposal §2.7 round-trip
# discipline ("round-trips per @io/secrets.round_trip discipline").
#
# Returns imperfect<verdict, ref, ref>. On success: verdict is
# Pass iff round-trip preserved bytes.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
sops_round_trip(section: ref, key_group: sops_key_group, k: key_material) -> imperfect { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The bilaterals (Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude)
# ============================================================

# === sops_key_group_admissible predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a sops_key_group is well-formed:
#
#   1. Combined recipient set (age ∪ pgp ∪ kms) is non-empty.
#   2. Every age recipient passes @io/crypto.recipients_admissible.
#   3. Every PGP fingerprint resolves to a keyring entry (via
#      the realisation boundary; substrate carries only the ref).
#   4. Every KMS recipient is a well-formed backend URI/ARN.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude per Mara-B §4.5.5: reads only
# byte-visible recipient strings + list lengths; no program
# semantics.
#
# Splinter-pole: key group is well-formed; sops_encrypt would
# produce decryptable ciphertext.
# Narcissus-pole: empty recipient set, malformed recipient,
# unreachable keyring; encryption would silently succeed with
# undecryptable output OR fail at runtime.
sops_key_group_admissible(kg: sops_key_group) -> verdict { \ }

# === sops_metadata_valid predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that a sops_metadata carrier is substrate-
# honest:
#
#   1. key_group passes sops_key_group_admissible.
#   2. integrity_mac is well-formed per SOPS integrity discipline
#      (SHA512 HMAC byte-length; algorithm ref admissible).
#   3. encryption_policy is a well-formed regex pair (encrypted_
#      regex + unencrypted_regex; mutually exclusive per SOPS
#      discipline).
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible
# metadata fields; no program semantics.
#
# Splinter-pole: metadata is well-formed; SOPS binary would
# accept the file.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-check fails.
sops_metadata_valid(m: sops_metadata) -> verdict { \ }

# === sops_round_trip_preserved predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that sops_encrypt ∘ sops_decrypt on a section
# returns byte-equal plaintext. THE structural discipline
# distinguishing honest SOPS discharge from Narcissus-pole (claimed
# encryption that alters bytes on decrypt).
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads byte-visible plaintext
# state before + after round-trip; equality check is bounded.
#
# Splinter-pole: bytes round-trip cleanly.
# Narcissus-pole: bytes altered (YAML/JSON key reordering not
# preserved; encoding drift; leaf-value normalization).
sops_round_trip_preserved(section: ref, kg: sops_key_group, k: key_material) -> verdict { \ }

# === sops_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at @io/secrets/sops
# altitude. Composes:
#
#   1. sops_metadata_valid(f.metadata)
#   2. fs_well_formed(f.on_disk_path) — @io/fs disk-side
#      admissibility (composed transitively via @io/secrets).
#   3. sops_key_group_admissible(f.metadata.key_group).
#
# Sibling to @io/secrets.secrets_well_formed, @io/oci.oci_well_
# formed, @io/git.git_well_formed, @io/algebra.io_algebra_well_
# formed, @io/crypto.crypto_well_formed, @io/fs.fs_well_formed —
# the composed-bilateral pattern at @io species altitude.
#
# Splinter-pole: SOPS file is well-formed across metadata,
# disk-side, and recipient discipline.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-check fails; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics (#57) distinguishes which claim broke.
sops_well_formed(f: sops_file_ref) -> verdict
requires sops_metadata_valid(f.metadata)
{ \ }

out @io/secrets/sops
out sops_file_ref
out sops_key_group
out sops_metadata
out sops_encrypt
out sops_decrypt
out sops_key_group_from_sheaf_restriction
out sops_round_trip
out sops_key_group_admissible
out sops_metadata_valid
out sops_round_trip_preserved
out sops_well_formed
